WEBVTT

00:15.724 --> 00:17.934
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:19.394 --> 00:22.313
EPISODE 4

00:28.862 --> 00:30.447
FOCUS ON YOUR EMOTIONS AND PICK 1 CARD

00:30.530 --> 00:31.906
REVERSED WHEEL OF FORTUNE

00:31.990 --> 00:35.160
"The Reversed
Wheel of Fortune Card indicates

00:36.661 --> 00:40.081
a confusing situation
and approaching negative changes"?

01:07.859 --> 01:09.986
Damn it. What was it again?

01:10.070 --> 01:13.865
I didn't even get to watch their surgery,
so what more am I supposed to write?

01:17.535 --> 01:20.455
Didn't they order
a placenta pathology for this surgery?

01:21.122 --> 01:22.624
Then it should've been marked.

01:23.333 --> 01:25.001
You're right. What?

01:25.877 --> 01:27.087
You're a genius.

01:27.170 --> 01:28.963
Didn't they also put
a balloon in the uterus?

01:29.047 --> 01:30.048
That's missing too.

01:30.715 --> 01:31.591
Right.

01:33.510 --> 01:36.721
And I noticed earlier that
there was a typo in Ms. Kim Sin-u's chart.

01:36.805 --> 01:38.807
Where? I read it all.

01:40.016 --> 01:41.643
It was near the middle.

01:41.726 --> 01:43.353
That one. "Doppler."

01:43.436 --> 01:45.188
D-O-P-P-L… It's correct.

01:45.271 --> 01:49.859
"D" should be capitalized
since it's derived from a person's name.

01:53.071 --> 01:54.572
Yes. You're right.

01:55.365 --> 01:57.033
I appreciate it. Thanks.

02:02.497 --> 02:04.415
I don't want you to get scolded again.

02:04.958 --> 02:06.751
It's pretty hard to watch that.

02:07.919 --> 02:09.337
Ask me anytime.

02:09.420 --> 02:11.923
I like teaching and helping others.

02:12.465 --> 02:14.175
You'll be able to do it well soon.

02:14.259 --> 02:15.301
Sure. Okay.

02:18.930 --> 02:21.558
Arriving at the lobby in five minutes.
Don't be late.

02:22.725 --> 02:24.352
Geez, why is she here?

02:25.019 --> 02:26.396
Hey, it's finally out!

02:26.479 --> 02:27.313
What is that?

02:28.606 --> 02:29.482
Ta-da.

02:30.191 --> 02:31.067
Check this out.

02:33.027 --> 02:34.279
Don't we look good? Look.

02:35.196 --> 02:36.197
Yi-young.

02:36.781 --> 02:38.324
She was just being herself.

02:38.908 --> 02:40.577
She never listens.

02:40.660 --> 02:42.287
You should've posed properly.

02:42.370 --> 02:44.122
Who does an old-school jump shot
these days?

02:44.205 --> 02:45.957
Don't you know classics are timeless?

02:46.541 --> 02:49.085
You were embarrassed then,
but aren't you glad you took it?

02:49.169 --> 02:50.253
If it wasn't for me,

02:50.336 --> 02:53.214
you guys would've missed out
on these first-year memories.

02:53.965 --> 02:56.467
Let's take one every year.

02:57.051 --> 02:58.261
And in our second year…

02:59.012 --> 02:59.929
Someone's calling.

03:02.432 --> 03:04.809
OH JOO-YOUNG

03:07.186 --> 03:08.021
I'm going now.

03:10.982 --> 03:12.317
I'll be right back.

03:12.400 --> 03:14.027
-Where are you going?
-To meet someone.

03:14.110 --> 03:15.820
-Who?
-You don't need to know.

03:16.946 --> 03:18.531
Geez, you're so curious.

03:19.407 --> 03:22.035
She always leaves
whenever we mention "second year."

03:31.544 --> 03:33.463
Right, I forgot the adhesion barrier.

03:38.301 --> 03:39.636
She didn't log out.

03:45.934 --> 03:48.353
Bring your friends. I'll treat them.

03:48.436 --> 03:51.564
I told you we're not friends.
We're just coworkers.

03:52.106 --> 03:54.108
Why make friends when I'm quitting soon?

03:57.487 --> 03:59.405
Geez, you're impossible.

03:59.489 --> 04:01.491
No wonder you never have friends.

04:02.075 --> 04:03.993
I really can't do this anymore.

04:06.162 --> 04:07.330
That's enough.

04:08.039 --> 04:10.541
Really? Then should I quit today?

04:10.625 --> 04:11.542
Or tomorrow?

04:12.210 --> 04:13.711
She doesn't mean it.

04:13.795 --> 04:16.005
We all keep a resignation letter handy.

04:16.089 --> 04:16.923
What for?

04:19.842 --> 04:22.762
Let her be. She'll be the only one
who loses out if she quits.

04:22.845 --> 04:23.972
Why should I care?

04:24.055 --> 04:25.765
Let her be
a third-time resident applicant.

04:26.724 --> 04:28.351
I hope she doesn't quit.

04:28.434 --> 04:30.937
I could help her
with charting and study sessions.

04:31.020 --> 04:32.855
Hey! Me too!

04:33.439 --> 04:36.985
Help me out too. I think I'll get fired
even before I write my resignation letter.

04:37.068 --> 04:39.237
They're short on residents.
I doubt you'll get fired.

04:41.114 --> 04:41.948
I see.

04:43.449 --> 04:45.702
You only speak facts, don't you?

04:48.371 --> 04:50.581
You guys speak
completely different languages.

04:50.665 --> 04:52.667
No wonder you can't communicate.

04:53.376 --> 04:54.961
-You startled me.
-Oh Yi-young!

04:55.044 --> 04:56.296
Did she throw this away?

04:57.213 --> 04:59.590
I worked hard to print this.

04:59.674 --> 05:01.467
She must've dropped it while leaving.

05:03.177 --> 05:04.804
You can comfort others too.

05:09.934 --> 05:12.312
Who said anything
about quitting right now?

05:13.146 --> 05:15.940
Every resident thinks about quitting.

05:16.524 --> 05:17.400
Right?

05:18.234 --> 05:21.612
You do have an ounce of conscience
and a tiny bit of common sense, don't you?

05:21.696 --> 05:23.364
Of course I do.

05:23.448 --> 05:25.783
Come on. I wouldn't be able to do
this job otherwise.

05:27.577 --> 05:29.537
It's unlike you to splurge like this.

05:30.413 --> 05:31.289
I didn't pay.

05:31.372 --> 05:32.707
Do-won did.

05:33.583 --> 05:35.168
This one's their signature cake.

05:35.668 --> 05:37.670
This is the new release.
And what was this again?

05:38.254 --> 05:39.130
His favorite.

05:40.548 --> 05:43.176
Now that you work together,
you know his preferences too.

05:44.635 --> 05:45.803
It's my favorite too.

05:46.387 --> 05:48.973
Geez, you and your love for pastries.
Have it all.

05:54.687 --> 05:56.939
It would've been nice
if he'd eaten with us.

05:57.440 --> 06:00.485
He said he wasn't busy at all today
and told me to eat before leaving.

06:01.152 --> 06:03.780
-Maybe there's an emergency?
-I wouldn't be here in that case.

06:03.863 --> 06:04.697
Good point.

06:07.116 --> 06:08.951
-Did you say I was coming?
-You?

06:09.035 --> 06:10.203
Yes, I did.

06:12.246 --> 06:14.207
-Did you two fight?
-No.

06:14.290 --> 06:16.667
-He must've scolded you.
-No, he didn't.

06:16.751 --> 06:18.211
-Do your job well!
-I am!

06:18.294 --> 06:20.379
-How can I believe that?
-Think however you want.

06:20.463 --> 06:21.714
I didn't mean it anyway.

06:21.798 --> 06:24.425
You little… Unbelievable.

06:25.009 --> 06:26.219
Why are you here anyway?

06:27.762 --> 06:29.514
Did you actually come to check up on me?

06:29.597 --> 06:31.390
Yes, I came to see if you're behaving.

06:31.474 --> 06:34.602
Geez. I'm now 41.95 million won in debt.

06:34.685 --> 06:36.354
-Once I'm done--
-Okay.

06:36.437 --> 06:38.606
Focus on eating,
or you'll have an upset stomach.

06:54.705 --> 06:56.624
I'm thinking of trying again.

07:00.002 --> 07:01.003
Getting pregnant.

07:02.213 --> 07:04.298
I had a consultation
at the fertility center today.

07:04.882 --> 07:07.260
How come?
I thought you didn't want to try again.

07:07.343 --> 07:11.264
Now that six months have passed,
I have the desire to try again.

07:13.516 --> 07:15.143
I'm still thinking about it.

07:15.226 --> 07:18.604
It's a shame to give up
after only trying for four years.

07:20.106 --> 07:23.484
I want to try again before I hit 40.

07:24.902 --> 07:26.362
I haven't told Seung-won yet.

07:27.029 --> 07:27.905
It's a secret.

07:30.658 --> 07:31.576
Just…

07:32.618 --> 07:34.620
focus on raising me first.

07:34.704 --> 07:36.747
I'm still far from being a proper adult.

07:37.415 --> 07:38.458
So you're aware.

07:40.168 --> 07:41.752
HUSBAND

07:44.505 --> 07:45.715
Hi, honey.

07:47.717 --> 07:49.302
Yes, I stopped by the hospital.

07:49.802 --> 07:52.722
I saw Do-won briefly,
and now I'm with Yi-young.

07:53.806 --> 07:54.891
I asked.

07:56.100 --> 07:57.268
He said "no" to a blind date.

07:59.854 --> 08:02.148
I can't ask him that.

08:02.231 --> 08:04.233
You can ask. You're his brother.

08:07.487 --> 08:08.321
Yi-young?

08:09.280 --> 08:11.032
Okay. Bye.

08:13.117 --> 08:14.202
What blind date?

08:14.285 --> 08:17.205
Seung-won wanted to hook him up
with one of his coworkers.

08:17.788 --> 08:18.789
But Do-won refused.

08:19.540 --> 08:20.374
I see.

08:24.754 --> 08:26.839
Hey, by the way,

08:26.923 --> 08:28.925
is he seeing anyone at the hospital?

08:30.301 --> 08:32.553
I don't think so.

08:32.637 --> 08:34.180
Or…

08:35.014 --> 08:38.351
Maybe any rumors about him liking someone.
Does he not like anyone?

08:38.935 --> 08:39.769
I…

08:40.353 --> 08:41.187
don't think so.

08:42.104 --> 08:43.147
Wait.

08:43.231 --> 08:45.024
Does anyone like him?

08:45.107 --> 08:47.485
Did anyone say
that they're interested in him?

08:48.069 --> 08:49.403
I'm sure there's someone.

08:49.487 --> 08:50.655
Don't you know?

08:54.825 --> 08:56.077
There is one person.

08:57.870 --> 08:59.956
Right? There is someone, isn't there?

09:00.039 --> 09:00.873
Who is it?

09:02.375 --> 09:03.501
Who is it?

09:10.925 --> 09:12.134
Don't ask me.

09:13.135 --> 09:14.345
-How would I know?
-Hey!

09:15.680 --> 09:17.431
Geez. Did you have to shout?

09:17.515 --> 09:18.975
So do you know or not?

09:19.058 --> 09:20.142
I'm telling you to drop it.

09:20.226 --> 09:21.561
Are you serious right now?

09:25.398 --> 09:26.649
Thank you for calling.

09:27.692 --> 09:28.818
I'll be right there.

09:41.831 --> 09:45.042
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

09:58.389 --> 09:59.223
Who is it?

10:00.391 --> 10:02.768
Knock, knock. I heard the news.

10:02.852 --> 10:03.728
What news?

10:04.437 --> 10:07.273
That you have the same taste as me.

10:15.740 --> 10:16.657
I like women.

10:17.241 --> 10:18.492
What? Well…

10:19.076 --> 10:21.662
Me too. I like them a lot.

10:22.288 --> 10:24.999
That's not what I meant.
I heard you like tennis.

10:26.000 --> 10:27.752
I see. And?

10:28.419 --> 10:32.089
Why don't we create
a Yulje tennis team and meet up regularly?

10:32.673 --> 10:34.550
We could socialize and exercise.

10:34.634 --> 10:36.552
Befriending other departments
can't be bad.

10:38.137 --> 10:39.805
Every Friday at eight o'clock.

10:39.889 --> 10:41.057
Fridays don't work for me.

10:41.140 --> 10:42.725
Right. You're busy.

10:42.808 --> 10:43.934
Do it without me.

10:44.018 --> 10:46.270
How can we? You're the team chairman.

10:46.354 --> 10:47.563
OB-GYN
4TH-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE

10:47.647 --> 10:49.649
-Me?
-Yes, we all agreed on it.

10:50.733 --> 10:54.695
I wish it were some other day too,
but they're all free on Fridays.

10:54.779 --> 10:57.281
So just do it without me.
I'm busy on Fridays.

10:57.365 --> 10:59.533
I know. Everyone at the hospital knows.

11:00.201 --> 11:02.870
You eat Chinese food at the food court,

11:02.953 --> 11:05.247
organize the next week's surgeries
in the conference room,

11:05.331 --> 11:07.833
buy two cans of beer
at the convenience store on your way home,

11:07.917 --> 11:10.336
and then, tudum,
end your Friday night with Netflix.

11:10.419 --> 11:12.380
You live a boring,
lonely life, yet enjoy it.

11:12.463 --> 11:13.964
Mr. Boring Routine.

11:14.548 --> 11:15.549
We all know.

11:19.345 --> 11:20.429
It's super fun.

11:20.513 --> 11:23.265
That's what keeps me going.
I endure the whole week just to do that.

11:26.644 --> 11:28.771
Why am I wasting time
talking about this with you?

11:28.854 --> 11:30.981
Right. I'm sorry.

11:31.065 --> 11:33.317
If you're sorry, go do your job.

11:38.197 --> 11:39.323
I also need to go in--

11:39.407 --> 11:40.366
Go somewhere else.

11:40.449 --> 11:41.367
Should I do that?

11:45.121 --> 11:47.581
I'll see you later
in the sixth-floor conference room.

11:57.133 --> 11:58.426
The research topic is

11:58.509 --> 12:02.179
"predicting preterm birth
through cervical elasticity measurements."

12:02.263 --> 12:07.309
As of now, Dr. Ki and Dr. Park
are doing the research.

12:07.393 --> 12:09.019
I'd like one of you

12:09.562 --> 12:12.064
to handle
the statistical analysis of this data,

12:12.148 --> 12:15.234
oversee the overall progress,
and write the abstract.

12:16.360 --> 12:17.903
If it turns out well,

12:17.987 --> 12:20.072
we'll submit it to ISUOG

12:20.823 --> 12:23.451
which will be held in Italy this year.

12:23.534 --> 12:25.453
You'll be able to attend
a conference abroad.

12:26.787 --> 12:29.415
Your name will be listed
as the first author if you do well.

12:30.791 --> 12:32.668
You'll be learning a lot.

12:45.306 --> 12:47.641
Why don't you give it a try, Yi-young?

12:50.561 --> 12:51.395
Me?

12:53.772 --> 12:54.607
I…

12:58.819 --> 13:01.822
I don't have the ability
or diligence for that.

13:03.365 --> 13:04.283
I'm sorry.

13:04.366 --> 13:06.076
We won't know until you try.

13:06.952 --> 13:08.871
Judging by your face, you seem interested.

13:08.954 --> 13:09.872
Right?

13:13.375 --> 13:14.251
Okay.

13:15.002 --> 13:16.629
I'll give it a try.

13:16.712 --> 13:18.672
She'll write the first paper.

13:19.173 --> 13:22.092
Then Sa-bi, Nam-kyung, and Jae-il
will write in this order.

13:22.593 --> 13:24.261
-Got it?
-Yes, ma'am.

13:25.179 --> 13:28.849
Please email me a summary
of the progress of your assigned research

13:28.933 --> 13:29.934
at the end of each month.

13:30.017 --> 13:30.851
Yes, ma'am.

13:32.353 --> 13:35.105
Gosh, Professor Seo is so eloquent.

13:35.189 --> 13:38.317
I mean, I was raising my hand
before I even knew it.

13:38.400 --> 13:40.819
I was totally persuaded
when she mentioned Italy.

13:40.903 --> 13:43.447
When I came to my senses,
my hand was already up.

13:44.490 --> 13:45.991
But how will I make time for it?

13:46.075 --> 13:48.285
Why did she ask us
to raise our hand anyway?

13:49.119 --> 13:50.746
Wasn't she looking for volunteers?

13:51.247 --> 13:52.248
This is so unfair.

13:52.331 --> 13:54.667
You're right. It's completely unfair.

13:54.750 --> 13:55.584
Exactly.

13:56.126 --> 13:59.213
Why give the opportunity
to someone who wants to quit?

14:03.926 --> 14:07.096
What a waste of opportunity.

14:08.847 --> 14:09.723
Hey.

14:16.355 --> 14:18.274
We didn't mean to pry.

14:18.899 --> 14:20.568
You didn't log out when you left.

14:22.027 --> 14:25.406
Sa-bi is just upset
since you said you're quitting.

14:25.489 --> 14:27.408
I know you didn't mean it.

14:28.534 --> 14:30.035
We're friends, so please understand.

14:30.119 --> 14:33.372
Understand what?
That she's upset because I said I'd quit?

14:34.540 --> 14:36.834
That sounds like an excuse to me.

14:36.917 --> 14:40.337
Or that she's upset
since I'm doing the paper?

14:41.463 --> 14:42.506
Both.

14:42.590 --> 14:44.341
That's not true. It's the latter.

14:45.175 --> 14:46.594
She's upset over nothing.

14:47.803 --> 14:50.806
I have a hair appointment.
Bye. Good luck with your shift.

14:52.349 --> 14:53.183
Good luck.

15:00.274 --> 15:01.150
Hello.

15:01.984 --> 15:03.027
Hello.

15:04.987 --> 15:06.071
I'm sorry.

15:06.155 --> 15:09.033
I'm so used to wearing my surgery gown.

15:09.116 --> 15:10.743
I see. You must be a doctor.

15:10.826 --> 15:11.660
Yes, I am.

15:12.161 --> 15:16.040
-You must've set aside some time to come.
-Yes, I barely managed to make time.

15:19.919 --> 15:20.961
Yes?

15:21.045 --> 15:23.589
Dr. Pyo, it's about Ms. Kim Hyeong-ja.

15:23.672 --> 15:26.467
You prescribed an NSAID,
but she says she's allergic to it.

15:26.550 --> 15:29.011
I think you need to prescribe
a different painkiller.

15:30.137 --> 15:32.556
Then give her acetaminophen.

15:32.640 --> 15:34.516
I'll type up the prescription myself.

15:34.600 --> 15:35.935
I'm sorry for the hassle.

15:36.936 --> 15:39.313
Okay. Sorry.

15:42.524 --> 15:45.027
Dr. Pyo, that's not how you should work.

15:45.110 --> 15:46.695
What? Hello, ma'am.

15:47.404 --> 15:49.907
It doesn't seem like a big deal,
so why are you sorry?

15:49.990 --> 15:50.824
Sorry?

15:51.951 --> 15:53.202
Was that a nurse?

15:53.285 --> 15:54.370
Yes.

15:54.453 --> 15:55.913
It's May already.

15:55.996 --> 15:57.915
You should stop being a pushover.

15:59.583 --> 16:01.585
You're a resident after all.

16:01.669 --> 16:02.503
Right.

16:03.379 --> 16:04.505
But what about it?

16:09.635 --> 16:12.680
Thank you for teaching me
so much, Dr. Myeong.

16:13.305 --> 16:14.723
It's nothing, really.

16:14.807 --> 16:16.892
I just wanted to introduce
some new hair products.

16:16.976 --> 16:18.435
Don't you think you bought too much?

16:18.519 --> 16:20.980
I realized I needed all of them.

16:21.647 --> 16:23.232
Thank goodness we bought this shampoo.

16:23.899 --> 16:26.777
I put in plenty of samples
for you to use at the hospital.

16:26.860 --> 16:27.861
Really?

16:28.404 --> 16:29.488
Thank you.

16:30.072 --> 16:31.532
Thank you. I'll come again.

16:31.615 --> 16:32.533
Goodbye.

16:32.616 --> 16:34.326
-Thank you
-Goodbye.

16:40.666 --> 16:43.544
They're so not street-smart, are they?

16:44.628 --> 16:47.923
Gosh, should I have bought
another conditioner?

16:48.007 --> 16:50.092
I agree. We could've just stocked up.

16:50.175 --> 16:51.010
Exactly.

16:51.552 --> 16:53.971
-I'm headed that way.
-I'm taking the subway.

16:54.054 --> 16:55.139
Okay. Bye.

16:55.222 --> 16:56.557
Get home safe.

17:02.187 --> 17:05.524
Do you think Yi-young will really quit?

17:05.607 --> 17:07.359
I told you she didn't mean it.

17:07.943 --> 17:10.779
I told you that
people don't always mean what they say.

17:12.281 --> 17:14.908
She should just quit already
if she's going to anyway,

17:15.409 --> 17:17.494
so I can work on Professor Seo's paper.

17:46.190 --> 17:48.776
-Who is it?
-Sir, it's Oh Yi-young, first-year.

17:54.865 --> 17:57.159
-What is it? An emergency?
-No, it's not.

17:57.743 --> 17:58.952
I'm on call today,

17:59.036 --> 18:01.246
and I didn't want to
call the professor at this hour.

18:02.081 --> 18:03.540
I just need your confirmation.

18:03.624 --> 18:04.625
Sure.

18:04.708 --> 18:07.461
Patient Woo Jeong-hyo's water broke
about ten hours ago.

18:07.544 --> 18:09.171
Should I start antibiotics?

18:09.254 --> 18:10.422
What's her temperature?

18:10.506 --> 18:11.965
It's 37°C.

18:13.967 --> 18:16.887
Let's wait a bit longer
and start once it's been 12 hours.

18:17.888 --> 18:20.474
And Ms. Kang Hyeon-yeong
who had postpartum hemorrhage.

18:20.557 --> 18:23.685
Her hemoglobin level is 10 g/dL.
When should we follow up?

18:24.353 --> 18:25.187
She's…

18:25.854 --> 18:27.898
Is she Professor Seo's patient
from today's surgery?

18:27.981 --> 18:28.816
Correct.

18:30.901 --> 18:32.569
-Let's do it on POD 2.
-Okay.

18:33.153 --> 18:33.987
One more thing.

18:35.030 --> 18:36.990
This one feels weak
because she hasn't eaten yet.

18:37.074 --> 18:38.826
She can't eat now
as no restaurant is open.

18:38.909 --> 18:40.160
What should we do?

18:40.911 --> 18:42.412
-Who is she?
-Me.

18:49.294 --> 18:56.260
OB-GYN
4TH-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE

18:56.343 --> 18:58.262
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

18:59.930 --> 19:00.806
Hello.

19:01.306 --> 19:03.267
Sa-bi, you're early today.

19:03.350 --> 19:04.768
This is when I always come.

19:04.852 --> 19:05.769
I see.

19:05.853 --> 19:08.313
And breakfast? Let's go
to the convenience store and--

19:08.397 --> 19:09.731
I always have this.

19:10.399 --> 19:11.441
I see.

19:11.525 --> 19:12.985
You're well-prepared.

19:13.068 --> 19:14.736
Okay. I'll see you later then.

19:16.071 --> 19:17.865
Okay. Bye.

19:24.621 --> 19:25.455
Hi.

19:27.040 --> 19:28.041
Hey, you're here.

19:35.757 --> 19:36.967
Can you stop shaking your leg?

19:38.218 --> 19:39.052
What?

19:39.928 --> 19:41.013
Right. Okay.

19:41.555 --> 19:42.931
And that's my pen.

19:46.059 --> 19:47.686
Okay. Sorry.

19:54.276 --> 19:55.444
By the way…

19:59.740 --> 20:00.574
Yes, ma'am.

20:02.242 --> 20:04.453
I'm reviewing Ms. Hwangbo Bo-hyeon's case.

20:05.120 --> 20:05.954
Me?

20:06.747 --> 20:08.207
I've never done that before--

20:09.708 --> 20:11.001
Today will be my first.

20:12.711 --> 20:13.629
Yes, ma'am.

20:17.925 --> 20:19.134
Was that Professor Seo?

20:19.218 --> 20:21.470
Yes, there's a multidisciplinary
prenatal consultation with CS.

20:21.553 --> 20:22.679
She wants me to explain it.

20:22.763 --> 20:24.056
A multidisciplinary consultation?

20:25.557 --> 20:27.559
I didn't know
first-years got to attend them.

20:27.643 --> 20:28.810
Me neither.

20:28.894 --> 20:29.728
What for?

20:29.811 --> 20:31.813
Because of the mother? Or the baby?

20:31.897 --> 20:35.025
She's a mother who had a stillbirth
at 32 weeks due to Ebstein anomaly.

20:35.108 --> 20:37.778
The same anomaly was detected again
in the recent ultrasound.

20:38.278 --> 20:40.906
Those cases are very rare.

20:40.989 --> 20:42.741
Will they do an amniotic fluid test?

20:42.824 --> 20:44.284
Don't tell me you're assisting.

20:45.077 --> 20:46.203
I wouldn't know.

20:50.374 --> 20:53.210
Have you read any papers
on fetal Ebstein anomaly?

20:54.002 --> 20:55.212
Or maybe in a textbook?

20:58.882 --> 21:00.884
I don't know everything.

21:02.678 --> 21:03.553
That's true.

21:08.600 --> 21:09.434
Yes?

21:10.227 --> 21:11.103
I'm on my way.

21:18.777 --> 21:20.195
Damn it. Whatever.

21:26.285 --> 21:28.578
CERTIFICATE OF COMMENDATION

21:30.080 --> 21:31.915
Twenty weeks and how many days?

21:35.043 --> 21:36.837
It's been 20 weeks and two days.

21:36.920 --> 21:38.213
What about the first pregnancy?

21:39.089 --> 21:40.924
I wasn't here then,

21:41.508 --> 21:42.759
so I'm not sure.

21:47.639 --> 21:49.057
How is that an excuse?

21:49.141 --> 21:50.559
I'm sorry.

21:51.226 --> 21:53.061
During her first pregnancy in 2021,

21:53.145 --> 21:56.189
Ebstein anomaly was detected
during the 20-week detailed ultrasound.

21:56.273 --> 21:58.191
The pregnancy continued
but ended in stillbirth.

21:58.275 --> 21:59.109
At that time--

21:59.192 --> 22:01.361
Her first pregnancy,
so an amniocentesis wasn't performed?

22:01.445 --> 22:02.321
Yes, that's correct.

22:02.404 --> 22:03.655
It's all in the record.

22:03.739 --> 22:05.782
How is the attending doctor
explaining this to me

22:06.283 --> 22:08.285
without properly understanding
her own patient?

22:10.537 --> 22:11.538
I'm sorry.

22:11.621 --> 22:13.040
What's the issue with the heart?

22:14.666 --> 22:17.294
The tricuspid valve position is abnormal,
so the left ventricle--

22:17.377 --> 22:18.211
Right ventricle.

22:20.547 --> 22:21.506
Right.

22:23.550 --> 22:26.053
The right ventricle is small,
and the blood…

22:30.974 --> 22:32.976
-flows back to the left atrium--
-Right atrium.

22:33.477 --> 22:36.021
Pressure in the right atrium
is causing the atrial hypertrophy.

22:36.104 --> 22:37.230
Right.

22:37.314 --> 22:39.900
How will the guardian understand
and give you their consent

22:40.400 --> 22:43.028
when you know so little
about your patient's case?

22:43.612 --> 22:44.613
I'm sorry.

22:45.739 --> 22:47.407
-You're here.
-Hey. Delivery?

22:47.491 --> 22:48.825
Yes. Sorry.

22:51.661 --> 22:52.537
Hey.

22:53.538 --> 22:56.041
Why are you grilling
my resident at my hospital?

22:56.124 --> 22:59.127
I wasn't grilling her.
I just asked a few questions.

22:59.211 --> 23:02.005
I'll take care of my residents.
You just worry about CS.

23:02.089 --> 23:03.632
I have no residents to worry about.

23:03.715 --> 23:06.676
We got three newbies this year,
and I haven't seen one in days.

23:07.177 --> 23:08.678
I don't know. Whatever.

23:08.762 --> 23:10.180
You're envious, aren't you?

23:12.307 --> 23:13.350
Yes, of just one of them.

23:14.184 --> 23:15.185
Thanks for coming.

23:15.685 --> 23:18.063
Our pediatric thoracic surgeon,
Professor Cha Byeong-seon,

23:18.146 --> 23:19.481
wanted you to take a look.

23:19.564 --> 23:20.774
Yes, he called.

23:21.858 --> 23:23.276
Take a look at this.

23:26.113 --> 23:28.865
Ebstein anomaly was detected
during the 19-week detailed ultrasound

23:28.949 --> 23:30.158
of Ms. Hwangbo Bo-hyeon.

23:30.242 --> 23:33.036
We're planning to perform
an amniocentesis for genetic testing

23:33.120 --> 23:34.246
during her next visit.

23:34.746 --> 23:38.083
The same heart defect was found
during her first pregnancy two years ago.

23:38.166 --> 23:41.419
We couldn't determine the genetic cause
since genetic testing wasn't performed.

23:41.920 --> 23:43.463
She had a stillbirth at 32 weeks.

23:44.422 --> 23:46.049
The heart defect is identical.

23:48.260 --> 23:50.554
I hope the baby weighs
at least 2.7 kg at birth.

23:51.513 --> 23:54.182
The surgery will be riskier
if the baby is too small.

23:54.266 --> 23:55.350
I think we can manage

23:55.433 --> 23:58.228
if there is no heart failure
or cardiomegaly until 34 weeks.

23:58.311 --> 23:59.229
What's your take?

23:59.771 --> 24:02.399
It's a milder type
compared to two years ago.

24:02.482 --> 24:04.985
The blood is flowing well
through the pulmonary artery.

24:05.569 --> 24:07.988
The baby is growing appropriately
for gestational age.

24:09.489 --> 24:12.701
But it's still only 20 weeks,
so we need to monitor longer.

24:13.285 --> 24:15.662
Schedule a consultation with the mother.
I'll be there.

24:15.745 --> 24:18.373
Let's discuss the results
in the next multidisciplinary meeting.

24:18.456 --> 24:19.416
Got it.

24:19.499 --> 24:21.126
MULTIDISCIPLINARY: MULTIPLE DEPARTMENTS

24:21.209 --> 24:23.712
Let's do well
so we can drink that this time.

24:26.464 --> 24:27.757
Yes, if it pans out,

24:29.092 --> 24:30.093
then we'll open it.

24:36.016 --> 24:37.434
Okay, that's it for the day.

24:37.976 --> 24:39.269
Now that we're done, applaud!

24:53.700 --> 24:54.993
I'm sorry.

24:55.076 --> 24:56.203
Dr. Oh.

24:56.286 --> 24:59.247
We're discussing a life-and-death issue,
and you're sleepy?

25:00.040 --> 25:00.999
I'm sorry.

25:01.958 --> 25:04.044
I was on call yesterday
and couldn't sleep at all.

25:04.127 --> 25:06.046
Right, you don't sleep
when you're on call,

25:06.129 --> 25:07.964
and you're expected to work the next day.

25:08.465 --> 25:09.299
Yes, sir.

25:10.508 --> 25:12.928
You remind me a lot of someone.

25:13.678 --> 25:16.181
There's this guy
who always has something to say

25:16.264 --> 25:18.725
even when he makes

25:19.643 --> 25:20.477
mistakes.

25:22.229 --> 25:23.188
Speak of the devil.

25:24.189 --> 25:27.525
What is it now, Dr. Do Jae-hak?
This is your third time calling today.

25:28.193 --> 25:31.321
I just have a question.
It's about my patient, Ms. Kim Jin-hee.

25:31.404 --> 25:32.239
Okay.

25:34.491 --> 25:35.784
A shunt revision?

25:36.368 --> 25:37.410
-You can go.
-Okay.

25:37.494 --> 25:38.787
Yes.

25:40.205 --> 25:41.414
Is she on epinephrine?

25:41.915 --> 25:42.749
Okay.

25:45.418 --> 25:46.378
Here.

25:48.672 --> 25:50.882
You're slightly burning up.

25:51.466 --> 25:53.802
How come? I wonder why.

25:53.885 --> 25:56.596
An excellent doctor
will come to treat you in 30 minutes.

25:57.389 --> 25:59.140
Okay. Gosh.

26:00.475 --> 26:03.144
Please go down, fever.

26:03.228 --> 26:05.188
Hello.

26:05.272 --> 26:06.523
Hello.

26:09.442 --> 26:12.737
What are you doing?

26:13.530 --> 26:14.447
Sorry?

26:16.992 --> 26:17.909
See?

26:18.535 --> 26:21.079
Even you can't hold onto them for long
since they're too cold.

26:21.162 --> 26:24.082
So what made you think
of putting them under her armpits?

26:24.165 --> 26:26.668
I'm sorry. She said her fever was rising.

26:26.751 --> 26:28.837
Of course her fever is rising.

26:28.920 --> 26:30.839
That's why she's getting chills!

26:30.922 --> 26:34.092
And yet you gave ice packs
to a patient with chills.

26:34.676 --> 26:37.721
Would you want these freezing ice packs
if you were her?

26:39.014 --> 26:39.848
No.

26:41.224 --> 26:44.519
Did you think putting those on her
and looking at her lovingly

26:44.602 --> 26:46.271
would make her fever go down?

26:46.980 --> 26:47.856
I'm sorry.

26:47.939 --> 26:49.816
You should've notified me!

26:50.400 --> 26:51.735
I knew you were coming soon.

26:52.444 --> 26:56.239
And her fever kept hovering around 37.7°C.

26:56.323 --> 26:58.116
The medication
wasn't really working either.

26:58.700 --> 27:00.660
I had to notify you to give an injection.

27:00.744 --> 27:01.911
But I couldn't do that

27:02.746 --> 27:05.749
because even I was unsure of myself. Well…

27:08.877 --> 27:12.005
I felt bad about calling you
so early in the morning.

27:12.088 --> 27:15.008
That's exactly why you shouldn't call
for unnecessary things.

27:15.091 --> 27:16.801
Call for urgent situations like this!

27:16.885 --> 27:18.553
Yes, it's my fault.

27:19.179 --> 27:20.013
I'm sorry.

27:20.764 --> 27:22.724
Seriously.

27:23.266 --> 27:24.601
Gosh, this is infuriating.

27:25.602 --> 27:28.355
You and your apologies.

27:30.273 --> 27:31.191
You'd better not.

27:33.777 --> 27:34.611
I'm sorry.

27:36.613 --> 27:39.240
Dr. Cha isn't someone
who gets annoyed by such calls.

27:40.367 --> 27:42.202
You could call her at dawn,

27:42.285 --> 27:44.079
and she'll still come right away.

27:44.704 --> 27:47.457
Everyone knows that. Didn't you know?

27:51.002 --> 27:53.254
Dr. Um, you made a mistake.

27:53.338 --> 27:55.840
Yes, it's my fault.

27:56.591 --> 27:59.928
We're waiting
for Dr. Um's prescription now.

28:00.804 --> 28:01.638
Really?

28:01.721 --> 28:03.348
We'll be quick.

28:04.516 --> 28:05.683
Dr. Um.

28:06.267 --> 28:08.186
I'm sorry, I'll do it right away.

28:24.411 --> 28:26.246
You're apologizing night and day.

28:28.164 --> 28:29.457
Gosh, you're an idiot.

28:30.083 --> 28:32.252
Yes. I am an idiot.

28:33.211 --> 28:36.548
You're the reason
the nurses look down on us

28:36.631 --> 28:38.591
and dump their work on us.

28:43.805 --> 28:45.348
About that surgery note…

28:45.432 --> 28:46.516
Yes, Doctor.

28:46.599 --> 28:49.811
They were twins,
but you wrote it on the singleton form.

28:50.729 --> 28:51.604
Me?

28:52.230 --> 28:53.273
Did I do that?

28:53.356 --> 28:56.109
Yes, could you rewrite it
on the form for twins?

28:56.192 --> 28:58.903
I'll fix it right away. I'm sorry.

28:58.987 --> 29:01.656
No, it's not your fault.
The file format was wrong.

29:01.740 --> 29:03.158
The content was pretty good.

29:03.241 --> 29:04.242
I see.

29:04.325 --> 29:05.660
Right, Ms. Min Ju-hee.

29:05.744 --> 29:08.163
She also had twins
after a salpingectomy just like this case,

29:08.246 --> 29:09.664
so use that as your reference.

29:09.748 --> 29:12.083
Yi-young wrote it,
and she did a pretty good job.

29:14.878 --> 29:15.795
Okay.

29:15.879 --> 29:17.964
By the way, have you eaten?

29:18.047 --> 29:20.425
I left some pizza
in the on-call room, so have some--

29:20.508 --> 29:23.720
Thank you, but I have no appetite.

29:24.971 --> 29:26.055
Goodbye.

29:31.394 --> 29:33.396
I taught her how to do this.

29:53.416 --> 29:55.919
AUTHOR: R1 OH YI-YOUNG
SAVE EMPTY DOCUMENT 1?

30:14.979 --> 30:16.481
How could you lose the data?

30:17.315 --> 30:19.984
Everyone has wasted their time
this morning, thanks to you.

30:20.068 --> 30:21.236
What have you done?

30:21.319 --> 30:22.862
The Witch has exploded again.

30:24.072 --> 30:25.615
I can't hear anything.

30:26.324 --> 30:27.492
So why am I sweating?

30:29.035 --> 30:30.745
I was happy
about the study being canceled.

30:30.829 --> 30:31.830
I feel bad now.

30:31.913 --> 30:33.998
Yi-young has definitely lost interest.

30:34.082 --> 30:36.292
I mean, how could you lose the data?

30:37.418 --> 30:39.712
Professor Seo won't let this one slide.

30:39.796 --> 30:43.800
It's either "You're banned from the OR"
or "Don't let me hear you breathing."

30:44.384 --> 30:45.760
I bet it's one of them.

30:45.844 --> 30:47.595
What? Aren't they the same thing?

30:48.847 --> 30:53.059
Then who'll assist
Professor Seo's surgery?

30:53.142 --> 30:54.811
-I'm not going.
-Me neither.

30:55.645 --> 30:57.188
We're busy in Gynecology.

30:57.939 --> 30:58.773
Then,

30:59.566 --> 31:00.441
should I go?

31:00.525 --> 31:01.359
Yes.

31:03.945 --> 31:05.572
God damn it.

31:06.281 --> 31:07.699
That stupid computer.

31:08.950 --> 31:10.493
I definitely did it before I left.

31:10.577 --> 31:11.661
Kim Sa-bi.

31:12.161 --> 31:13.496
You also saw it, didn't you?

31:13.580 --> 31:15.081
What? Yes.

31:15.748 --> 31:17.917
Why didn't you save it?

31:18.001 --> 31:20.879
We're grateful that
the study got canceled though.

31:20.962 --> 31:22.714
Hey, what did the professor say?

31:24.048 --> 31:26.885
I'm to prepare all the study materials
for the next three months.

31:28.845 --> 31:29.762
As for surgeries…

31:31.264 --> 31:32.682
I'm stuck with them forever.

31:32.765 --> 31:35.143
She wants me to attend
every single one of them.

31:35.226 --> 31:37.562
Geez. That's absolutely the worst.

31:39.314 --> 31:41.941
I don't know what to say to comfort you.

31:43.234 --> 31:44.235
Don't say anything.

31:44.944 --> 31:45.820
Okay.

32:14.933 --> 32:16.267
Let's say you comforted me too.

32:33.117 --> 32:34.327
I heard you got scolded again.

32:36.454 --> 32:37.497
I did.

32:37.580 --> 32:39.624
In my four years as a resident,

32:41.668 --> 32:44.629
I've never seen anyone
lose study materials.

32:45.171 --> 32:46.005
I didn't…

32:49.133 --> 32:50.301
I'm sorry.

32:50.885 --> 32:53.137
-Did you forget you were scolded?
-No, I didn't.

32:53.221 --> 32:54.430
I took her words to heart.

32:55.974 --> 32:56.891
Just brush it off.

32:59.102 --> 33:01.020
Forget about the scolding and focus.

33:01.729 --> 33:04.232
Make a mistake in here,
and it won't just end with a scolding.

33:04.857 --> 33:05.733
You know that, right?

33:08.277 --> 33:09.278
I do.

33:12.240 --> 33:13.116
Hello.

33:13.825 --> 33:16.661
The patient has
a history of two myomectomies,

33:16.744 --> 33:18.371
so there could be severe adhesions.

33:18.454 --> 33:20.873
-Make sure to maintain good visibility.
-Yes, ma'am.

33:20.957 --> 33:23.793
Do-won will make the uterine incision.

33:23.876 --> 33:24.836
Yes, ma'am.

33:29.549 --> 33:31.300
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

33:33.594 --> 33:35.304
Let's open the uterovesical serosa first.

33:35.388 --> 33:36.222
Yes, ma'am.

33:38.683 --> 33:40.226
Curvilinear on both sides.

33:40.309 --> 33:41.436
A CURVED LINE

33:44.188 --> 33:45.690
Push the serosa down.

34:03.791 --> 34:04.625
Okay.

34:05.209 --> 34:06.961
Let's make the uterine incision.

34:07.045 --> 34:07.879
Yes, ma'am.

34:15.803 --> 34:16.929
I'm so sorry.

34:17.013 --> 34:19.098
-Are you okay?
-Yes, the field is safe.

34:19.182 --> 34:22.018
Why was this upside down?

34:22.560 --> 34:24.312
What do I do? I'm really sorry!

34:24.896 --> 34:25.897
What should I do?

34:26.397 --> 34:27.774
What should I do? I'm sorry!

34:27.857 --> 34:29.317
That's enough. It's okay.

34:29.400 --> 34:30.276
Give me the scalpel.

34:32.403 --> 34:34.739
-Can you apply fundal with your left hand?
-Yes, ma'am.

34:34.822 --> 34:36.532
Let's get the baby out in one minute.

34:36.616 --> 34:38.951
Go straight to the ER
once we deliver the baby.

34:39.035 --> 34:40.161
Yes, ma'am.

34:42.663 --> 34:43.915
Remove the instrument.

34:46.250 --> 34:47.502
-Fundal.
-Yes, ma'am.

34:55.301 --> 34:56.511
The baby is out.

34:56.594 --> 34:57.804
Hi.

34:57.887 --> 34:59.555
It's a baby girl, born at 2:20 p.m.

35:11.442 --> 35:12.443
Good. You should go.

35:12.985 --> 35:14.737
-Make a call to the ER, please.
-Yes, ma'am.

35:14.821 --> 35:17.448
Will you be okay?
The bleeding seems to have stopped.

35:17.532 --> 35:19.742
It's okay. I have Yi-young.

35:20.660 --> 35:22.495
What are you doing? Switch places.

35:24.205 --> 35:25.039
Pardon?

35:29.168 --> 35:30.253
It's nothing serious.

35:30.920 --> 35:32.547
It happens often.

35:33.131 --> 35:35.925
The patient is the most important.
You know that, right?

35:36.843 --> 35:37.718
Yes, ma'am.

35:41.681 --> 35:42.515
Cut.

35:44.308 --> 35:45.893
Please give a pair to Dr. Oh too.

35:46.686 --> 35:47.520
Yes, ma'am.

35:52.316 --> 35:55.945
The patient plans to have a second child,
so we need to do a good suture.

35:56.571 --> 35:57.405
Yes, ma'am.

36:13.713 --> 36:15.548
-Pull a bit tighter.
-Yes, ma'am.

36:16.340 --> 36:20.553
Proper approximation
will prevent the tissue from separating.

36:20.636 --> 36:21.721
Yes, ma'am.

36:26.350 --> 36:28.436
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

36:37.862 --> 36:39.864
This is GYN Ward 101.

36:42.200 --> 36:43.201
I see.

36:43.993 --> 36:45.328
Okay, I understand.

36:45.411 --> 36:46.579
Goodbye.

36:48.539 --> 36:50.708
Doctor, it's Ms. Hwang Su-yeong
in Room 1018.

36:50.791 --> 36:52.001
Her SBP is 180.

36:52.084 --> 36:54.295
She's controlling her blood pressure
with beta blockers,

36:54.378 --> 36:55.922
so could you write a prescription?

36:59.300 --> 37:00.801
Dr. Pyo, the prescription…

37:04.889 --> 37:05.890
Dr. Pyo?

37:08.142 --> 37:08.976
Yes?

37:09.060 --> 37:11.229
Oh, you didn't hear me.

37:11.312 --> 37:13.898
Ms. Hwang Su-yeong's SBP is 180.

37:19.403 --> 37:23.032
Well… If you prescribe
beta blockers, I'll--

37:23.115 --> 37:24.033
I already did.

37:26.244 --> 37:28.579
I see. Thank you.

37:30.331 --> 37:31.332
One more thing.

37:32.124 --> 37:34.252
-Ms. Yang Jang-hee in Room 1012.
-Yes?

37:34.335 --> 37:36.337
Please check her I/O every two hours.

37:36.420 --> 37:37.421
Every two hours?

37:37.505 --> 37:40.132
I don't think
she needs that much monitoring.

37:40.216 --> 37:41.425
I've put in the order.

37:45.012 --> 37:45.930
Yes, ma'am.

38:03.281 --> 38:04.115
Doctor.

38:04.657 --> 38:06.867
It's a small cut.
Why are you wrapping it so much?

38:06.951 --> 38:08.411
Your mother called

38:08.494 --> 38:12.123
and demanded perfect treatment
both aesthetically and functionally.

38:12.206 --> 38:13.249
Mom? What mom?

38:13.833 --> 38:15.251
-Professor Seo.
-Geez.

38:17.253 --> 38:20.506
The person who did this
is going to feel extremely guilty.

38:21.632 --> 38:22.466
Do you think so?

38:27.972 --> 38:29.098
Can I help you?

38:30.224 --> 38:32.351
Oh, she's the guilty one.

38:32.435 --> 38:33.269
I see.

38:39.066 --> 38:40.234
I'm sorry.

38:40.818 --> 38:43.487
It's okay.
I also cut Professor Seo many times.

38:44.030 --> 38:45.364
These things happen sometimes.

38:47.825 --> 38:48.868
Does it hurt?

38:48.951 --> 38:49.785
No.

38:50.703 --> 38:51.537
Not one bit.

38:53.789 --> 38:56.876
Why do you feel so guilty?
I said I was fine.

38:59.337 --> 39:00.588
How's the patient?

39:01.797 --> 39:05.676
There was less bleeding than expected,
and her uterine contractions are normal.

39:05.760 --> 39:06.594
That's good.

39:08.512 --> 39:09.638
Did you assist well?

39:10.348 --> 39:12.224
Did you suture the wound nicely?

39:14.185 --> 39:15.061
Yes, sir.

39:17.480 --> 39:19.357
I'm truly sorry.

39:20.024 --> 39:22.651
I was focusing.
I just felt like I needed to do something.

39:22.735 --> 39:25.321
I was in a haste. I'm really sorry.

39:26.238 --> 39:29.575
I said I'm okay. I'm really fine. Just go.

39:29.658 --> 39:31.243
-Let me rest.
-Let me take a look.

39:31.327 --> 39:32.953
What's there to see? I'm okay, so go.

39:33.037 --> 39:34.622
-But I'm worried.
-It's fine.

39:34.705 --> 39:36.624
Obstetrics, quick. It's an emergency.

39:38.125 --> 39:39.627
AMBULANCE ENTRANCE ONLY

39:41.003 --> 39:42.129
119 EMERGENCY SERVICES

39:42.630 --> 39:44.298
She's 20 weeks pregnant. Her water broke.

39:44.382 --> 39:46.258
She was on her way here as an outpatient.

39:46.342 --> 39:47.593
Hwangbo Bo-hyeon, age 38.

39:47.676 --> 39:49.804
Current temperature, 39°C.
Blood pressure 90 over 60.

39:49.887 --> 39:51.138
This way, please.

39:51.222 --> 39:52.390
That's…

39:56.227 --> 39:57.436
Ms. Hwangbo Bo-hyeon

39:57.520 --> 39:59.647
was scheduled
for an amniocentesis this afternoon.

39:59.730 --> 40:00.940
But her water broke.

40:02.024 --> 40:03.567
There's almost no amniotic fluid left.

40:04.735 --> 40:06.821
We've canceled her scheduled test for now.

40:06.904 --> 40:07.738
Professor.

40:07.822 --> 40:11.033
The blood test result shows
that the WBC count is over 18,000,

40:11.117 --> 40:13.202
and the CRP has increased to 30.

40:13.285 --> 40:16.163
It appears the amniotic sac ruptured
due to chorioamnionitis.

40:16.789 --> 40:18.040
Her temperature is 40°C.

40:18.124 --> 40:20.292
Considering her blood pressure
isn't rising,

40:20.376 --> 40:22.920
it seems to have progressed to sepsis.

40:23.003 --> 40:23.963
I'm afraid…

40:27.174 --> 40:28.008
the baby…

40:43.607 --> 40:47.570
The chorioamnionitis infection
has spread within the uterus

40:48.320 --> 40:50.906
and is progressing
to a systemic infection.

40:53.033 --> 40:55.828
I'm afraid continuing the pregnancy
will be difficult.

40:55.911 --> 40:59.331
No, Doctor! I don't want that…

41:02.376 --> 41:04.712
The baby is currently
20 weeks and three days old.

41:05.421 --> 41:06.881
It's less than 300 grams.

41:07.465 --> 41:09.717
As you know,
the baby won't be able to survive

41:10.468 --> 41:11.844
even if it's born.

41:11.927 --> 41:16.140
Why is this happening to me?
What did I do wrong this time?

41:16.223 --> 41:17.057
Last time,

41:17.141 --> 41:20.186
the baby was fine until 32 weeks
despite a heart problem.

41:20.269 --> 41:23.147
You must be mistaken. I don't want to.

41:25.858 --> 41:26.775
Doctor.

41:29.403 --> 41:31.238
Just one day.

41:33.199 --> 41:35.868
Let me keep the baby
for just one more day.

41:37.453 --> 41:41.123
Please let me be a mother
for one more day.

41:42.291 --> 41:44.043
Only I can feel it.

41:45.711 --> 41:47.421
The baby is still alive.

41:48.214 --> 41:50.758
My baby can hold on, Doctor.

41:50.841 --> 41:53.427
You'll be at risk if the sepsis worsens.

41:54.762 --> 41:56.847
We need to proceed
with induced labor quickly--

41:56.931 --> 41:58.891
Please save my baby, Doctor.

41:58.974 --> 42:01.143
Please. Let me meet my baby.

42:01.227 --> 42:03.771
Please! I'll do anything!

42:04.813 --> 42:06.232
Let's stop here. Okay?

42:06.815 --> 42:07.691
Let's stop.

42:07.775 --> 42:09.902
I don't want to say goodbye again!

42:09.985 --> 42:12.780
I don't want to! I can't!

42:12.863 --> 42:14.073
Let's stop…

42:33.175 --> 42:34.260
I know it's difficult

42:35.177 --> 42:38.514
to cope with the process of letting go.

42:38.597 --> 42:39.807
But currently,

42:39.890 --> 42:43.394
vaginal delivery
is the best option for her.

42:43.477 --> 42:45.688
We'll proceed quickly with induced labor.

42:47.273 --> 42:48.315
Okay.

42:49.608 --> 42:51.277
Is it the same as before?

42:52.444 --> 42:53.279
Yes.

42:54.780 --> 42:55.864
And,

42:56.574 --> 42:58.784
regarding the baby's heart defect…

43:01.078 --> 43:02.746
Would you like to have it tested?

43:06.000 --> 43:06.959
My wife thinks

43:08.085 --> 43:10.296
that our previous baby didn't die.

43:11.547 --> 43:15.926
She thinks it just left for a while
and has returned again this time.

43:17.845 --> 43:20.806
She felt guilty
for sending the baby away all alone.

43:20.889 --> 43:23.392
She said she wanted to
meet the baby and apologize.

43:26.061 --> 43:29.064
Throughout her pregnancy,
she was too scared to sleep soundly.

43:31.650 --> 43:32.651
She'll probably

43:33.527 --> 43:35.654
want to meet the baby again.

43:39.950 --> 43:42.369
We'll do the test.

43:43.996 --> 43:45.414
My wife wants that as well,

43:46.498 --> 43:48.834
but she probably feels
too bad for the baby to say it.

43:50.002 --> 43:52.421
An amniocentesis isn't possible right now.

43:53.088 --> 43:56.925
We'll proceed with another test
as I explained before.

43:57.009 --> 44:00.763
These doctors
will explain everything again.

44:02.973 --> 44:04.016
Okay.

44:05.434 --> 44:06.268
By the way…

44:09.772 --> 44:10.856
Will it be painless?

44:11.440 --> 44:12.274
Yes.

44:13.484 --> 44:15.235
We'll prepare everything well.

44:25.204 --> 44:26.163
Do-won.

44:26.997 --> 44:29.917
Let's have Dr. Oh handle the tests

44:30.459 --> 44:31.669
for Ms. Hwangbo's baby.

44:32.670 --> 44:35.214
And have her practice suturing
when you have time.

44:35.297 --> 44:36.131
She has good hands.

44:36.215 --> 44:38.425
I want her to do
perineal suturing next time.

44:39.093 --> 44:40.761
Yes. Okay.

44:40.844 --> 44:43.347
I asked her to gather the research data.

44:43.972 --> 44:45.057
Don't worry about it.

44:45.724 --> 44:47.351
Yes. That's right.

44:47.434 --> 44:48.852
Okay. I'll be right there.

44:53.065 --> 44:56.652
Oh Yi-young, email me the references
on premature labor for the introduction

44:56.735 --> 44:58.529
by this afternoon.

45:03.325 --> 45:04.243
Yes, Doctor?

45:05.828 --> 45:09.581
Well… She kept getting angry
whenever I tried to do the pelvic exam.

45:12.626 --> 45:13.710
Yes, ma'am.

45:13.794 --> 45:15.921
I'll try to do it
without causing any pain.

45:16.755 --> 45:17.589
Goodbye.

45:28.100 --> 45:31.603
OH YI-YOUNG, EMAIL ME THE REFERENCES
ON PREMATURE LABOR FOR THE INTRODUCTION

45:31.687 --> 45:33.021
BY THIS AFTERNOON

45:56.879 --> 45:59.214
Over here! Please come quickly!

46:29.828 --> 46:31.663
Doctor, are you busy?

46:32.498 --> 46:33.499
Yes.

46:37.211 --> 46:39.671
It's about
Ms. Min Yeong-sil's surgery tomorrow.

46:39.755 --> 46:42.090
We're going to add antibiotics
to normal saline.

46:42.174 --> 46:43.675
Didn't I already order that?

46:44.843 --> 46:47.638
Yes, but usually,
antibiotics are mixed with 50 cc of NS.

46:47.721 --> 46:48.931
The prescription says 100 cc.

46:51.266 --> 46:52.726
Could you please modify it?

46:57.189 --> 46:58.398
Isn't it supposed to be 100?

46:59.066 --> 47:01.568
I'm sure it is. Geez.

47:03.820 --> 47:06.156
Okay, I understand.

47:12.746 --> 47:15.332
I've reordered it with 50 cc.

47:28.303 --> 47:30.722
Ta-da! Today seems quieter than--

47:30.806 --> 47:33.183
-Don't say that. Keep your mouth shut.
-Right.

47:34.059 --> 47:34.935
Okay.

47:36.812 --> 47:38.522
Nothing unusual in the ward, is there?

47:38.605 --> 47:40.148
Of course. There is something.

47:40.232 --> 47:41.858
What? What is it?

47:42.901 --> 47:44.903
-I got even for you.
-Even?

47:46.154 --> 47:48.824
To whom am I supposed to prescribe
an even number?

47:49.324 --> 47:51.577
No, not that kind of "even."

47:53.453 --> 47:55.372
-Nurse Ju-yeon.
-What?

47:55.455 --> 47:58.417
You guys were in there last time.

48:00.502 --> 48:01.545
In there?

48:02.254 --> 48:03.088
What?

48:05.007 --> 48:06.508
-What?
-What?

48:06.592 --> 48:07.426
What?

48:08.385 --> 48:09.761
-What?
-What are you saying?

48:10.387 --> 48:12.055
-What is this?
-What do you…

48:13.599 --> 48:14.933
Hey, Nurse Ju-yeon.

48:16.393 --> 48:18.145
-Don't you feel tired?
-Yes.

48:18.228 --> 48:21.231
Ta-da. There are almonds inside.

48:22.482 --> 48:23.317
Thank you.

48:24.109 --> 48:25.736
-Going to Room 1012?
-Yes.

48:25.819 --> 48:28.322
-Did the surgery go well?
-Yes, it was superfast.

48:32.326 --> 48:33.452
Yi-young.

48:34.077 --> 48:37.914
Professor Seo said to email the materials…

48:40.834 --> 48:41.877
What are you doing?

48:41.960 --> 48:42.919
Nothing.

48:44.046 --> 48:46.131
Geez. Greedy with food, aren't you?

48:48.091 --> 48:50.802
-By the way, have you seen Yi-young?
-Yes.

48:50.886 --> 48:53.013
Where is she? What's she doing?

48:53.096 --> 48:55.432
What else?
Getting an earful from Seo Jung-min again.

48:55.515 --> 48:57.225
-Why?
-Beats me.

48:58.518 --> 49:01.605
Seriously. How many times
has she been scolded?

49:02.105 --> 49:03.857
What if she really quits?

49:07.861 --> 49:09.488
Have you seen Jae-il?

49:09.571 --> 49:12.324
He said he was going to eat tteokbokki
with the nurses.

49:12.949 --> 49:14.409
But he can't even handle spicy food.

49:15.661 --> 49:18.205
You two must be close.
You even know his preference.

49:19.122 --> 49:20.040
Hardly.

49:20.624 --> 49:22.751
I believe he mentioned it before.

49:23.877 --> 49:24.711
Did he?

49:29.299 --> 49:31.009
Pyo Nam-kyung speaking.

49:33.303 --> 49:34.304
I'll be right there.

49:38.100 --> 49:40.769
I'm leaving. Enjoy your meal.

49:49.945 --> 49:51.363
-Doctor.
-Yes?

49:51.446 --> 49:52.864
-It's about Ms. Oh Mi-ok.
-Okay.

49:52.948 --> 49:55.867
She's getting her chemo right now
and feels very nauseous.

49:55.951 --> 49:59.579
I think you should check on her
before Professor Jo's rounds.

49:59.663 --> 50:00.497
Okay.

50:01.790 --> 50:02.833
Do you feel very nauseous?

50:04.501 --> 50:06.002
What if we stop the chemo for now,

50:06.086 --> 50:08.755
give her some hydration,
and administer an antiemetic?

50:10.590 --> 50:12.509
I'll give you an antiemetic first.

50:13.093 --> 50:14.219
For her next chemo session,

50:14.302 --> 50:16.471
let's use an antiemetic patch
the day before.

50:16.555 --> 50:17.556
Okay.

50:18.724 --> 50:20.809
The medication is almost finished though.

50:22.227 --> 50:23.395
It's okay.

50:23.478 --> 50:25.480
Throw up until you feel better. It's okay.

50:25.564 --> 50:26.398
Nurse Cho-won!

50:27.441 --> 50:28.275
Coming.

50:30.026 --> 50:30.944
-Please hold it.
-Okay.

50:39.202 --> 50:40.328
-Doctor.
-Yes?

50:40.412 --> 50:42.831
-I need an antiemetic prescription.
-Right. Okay.

50:44.124 --> 50:45.542
-I'll bring the medication.
-Okay.

50:55.385 --> 50:57.137
Nurse Cho-won,
I prescribed metoclopramide.

50:57.220 --> 50:58.138
Okay.

50:58.221 --> 51:00.015
MEDICATION USED FOR NAUSEA AND VOMITING

51:19.785 --> 51:21.787
Okay. I'll head up now.

51:24.164 --> 51:26.875
It's become such a habit for us
that our hands move automatically.

51:27.918 --> 51:31.129
Don't you feel better now?
You must've been so uncomfortable.

51:31.838 --> 51:32.964
Thank you.

51:33.882 --> 51:35.175
The medication is working well.

51:36.218 --> 51:38.303
I thought the cleaner would be here soon.

51:38.386 --> 51:42.349
I was worried about the other patients
in the room, so I just cleaned it up.

51:42.432 --> 51:44.100
There wasn't much to clean anyway.

51:45.060 --> 51:47.354
Professor Jo will give you an earful

51:47.437 --> 51:50.232
if he smells anything, you know?

51:50.816 --> 51:51.817
Right.

51:51.900 --> 51:55.654
I replaced the IV line since she had
to change her clothes. Please check.

51:59.574 --> 52:00.450
I'm sorry.

52:01.576 --> 52:03.078
I was the only one who didn't help.

52:04.204 --> 52:05.413
I was just doing my job.

52:06.790 --> 52:08.208
You should go get changed.

52:08.291 --> 52:10.502
I'll finish up here.

52:10.585 --> 52:13.630
Oh, but the professor will be here soon.

52:14.464 --> 52:15.882
Hello.

52:15.966 --> 52:16.883
Hello.

52:18.260 --> 52:19.094
What happened?

52:19.678 --> 52:22.222
I prescribed her metoclopramide
due to severe nausea.

52:22.305 --> 52:24.808
We replaced the IV line,
so I'm about to restart the pump.

52:24.891 --> 52:26.017
What's the ANC?

52:26.601 --> 52:28.854
Pardon? Right, it's…

52:31.690 --> 52:32.774
It's 2,500.

52:32.858 --> 52:33.775
Okay.

52:36.111 --> 52:37.988
Your immune function pre-chemo looks good.

52:38.071 --> 52:42.158
You're experiencing side effects
like nausea and digestive issues.

52:42.242 --> 52:46.746
But you'll feel significantly better
if we use antiemetics appropriately.

52:46.830 --> 52:51.042
If it's too difficult for you,
we can apply an antiemetic patch.

52:51.585 --> 52:53.086
Okay, I understand.

52:55.171 --> 53:00.385
OH YI-YOUNG, EMAIL ME THE REFERENCES

53:19.404 --> 53:20.739
Did you get scolded badly?

53:22.032 --> 53:25.994
Nam-kyung said
Professor Seo really gave you an earful.

53:27.120 --> 53:28.121
Right.

53:28.788 --> 53:30.707
She said you might even quit.

53:31.374 --> 53:32.500
I deserved it.

53:47.849 --> 53:48.934
Yi-young, listen.

53:50.226 --> 53:53.605
The professor left a note for you.

53:55.941 --> 53:58.610
Let's get it done right now.
She needs materials on--

53:58.693 --> 54:00.528
Preterm labor research references.

54:02.530 --> 54:03.657
I emailed them to her.

54:04.532 --> 54:06.534
Really? How?

54:07.410 --> 54:08.662
How did you know?

54:13.583 --> 54:14.626
Did you see?

54:16.086 --> 54:16.920
Yes.

55:00.380 --> 55:01.506
It was on the monitor.

55:02.507 --> 55:04.551
Someone must've put it back
after it fell.

55:04.634 --> 55:05.927
It was really dirty.

55:09.764 --> 55:10.765
I need water.

55:30.535 --> 55:31.369
You know what?

55:36.958 --> 55:39.127
I'll tell you why I got scolded again.

55:41.087 --> 55:43.423
A 20-week pregnant patient,
Ms. Hwangbo Bo-hyeon.

55:44.883 --> 55:47.886
We couldn't do an amniotic fluid test
since her water broke.

55:48.470 --> 55:50.472
So we decided to do a different test.

55:52.932 --> 55:54.476
But they told me to do it.

55:56.478 --> 55:57.520
So…

55:59.355 --> 56:00.648
I said I couldn't do it.

56:01.357 --> 56:03.276
And then, I got chewed out.

56:03.359 --> 56:04.194
Why?

56:04.986 --> 56:05.987
Why did you refuse?

56:06.821 --> 56:08.031
It's a good opportunity.

56:08.114 --> 56:11.201
The professor trusted you enough
to give you a chance, so you should do it.

56:11.993 --> 56:13.119
I mean…

56:13.620 --> 56:15.580
I'm not saying it's good news.

56:16.289 --> 56:18.541
But it can help the patient
with her future pregnancies

56:18.625 --> 56:21.086
and be used as a research case.

56:21.169 --> 56:22.420
Plus, it's a rare case.

56:23.088 --> 56:26.007
You get to learn, so that's good.

56:27.842 --> 56:31.096
It's for the patient and her future baby.

56:31.763 --> 56:33.098
You need to do it well.

56:35.642 --> 56:37.352
What's this? Am I talking to Seo Jung-min?

56:46.903 --> 56:48.404
So I'm going to do it now.

56:49.155 --> 56:51.741
She's being induced and will deliver soon.

56:53.451 --> 56:54.536
Speaking of which…

56:57.497 --> 56:58.581
Let's do it together.

57:04.504 --> 57:05.421
I'm scared.

57:15.265 --> 57:17.058
Please help me.

57:32.699 --> 57:36.035
Push on your lower abdomen,
and it'll hurt less.

57:38.538 --> 57:39.789
Yes, just a little more.

57:40.457 --> 57:41.291
A little more.

57:44.586 --> 57:45.670
It's out.

57:47.130 --> 57:49.007
Well done, ma'am.

57:49.632 --> 57:52.552
Now, we just need the placenta
to come out properly.

57:52.635 --> 57:54.137
Hang in there.

58:04.981 --> 58:06.232
Dr. Oh, I'll leave it to you.

58:08.067 --> 58:09.027
Ultrasound, please.

58:09.110 --> 58:10.028
Yes, ma'am.

58:10.111 --> 58:11.529
-Nurse Ji-young.
-Yes, ma'am.

58:13.364 --> 58:15.116
How are you feeling right now?

58:15.700 --> 58:17.076
Are you all right?

58:17.744 --> 58:18.578
Yes.

58:27.337 --> 58:28.213
Wait.

58:30.340 --> 58:31.174
The baby…

58:46.940 --> 58:47.774
I…

58:48.816 --> 58:51.110
I don't think I can do that test.

58:51.194 --> 58:52.028
And also…

58:53.363 --> 58:56.032
I can't do it alone.

58:56.115 --> 58:57.325
Then what should we do?

58:58.493 --> 59:01.412
We have three surgeries right now,
and Do-won is going into surgery too.

59:02.330 --> 59:04.749
Should we take the attending doctor off
and ask someone else?

59:06.543 --> 59:07.585
Dr. Oh.

59:07.669 --> 59:10.547
Whether we can do it or not
isn't for us to decide.

59:11.506 --> 59:13.925
The person struggling the most
right now is the patient,

59:14.008 --> 59:17.428
and she made the difficult decision
to go through with this.

59:18.555 --> 59:22.016
If it's for the mother and her baby,
we do it.

59:22.100 --> 59:23.560
That's not an acceptable excuse.

59:24.686 --> 59:25.937
But…

59:29.899 --> 59:31.150
Okay. I'm sorry.

59:31.943 --> 59:35.321
Ms. Hwangbo is starting to dilate,

59:35.405 --> 59:36.823
so keep a close eye on her.

59:37.323 --> 59:39.284
Call me when the delivery room is ready.

59:39.367 --> 59:41.160
Make sure the adjacent room
is also prepared.

59:45.873 --> 59:47.166
Good luck.

59:55.675 --> 59:56.509
Oh Yi-young.

59:58.886 --> 01:00:00.263
Do you have coins?

01:00:05.268 --> 01:00:06.144
Tell me.

01:00:07.604 --> 01:00:09.230
I saw this when I was an intern.

01:00:10.315 --> 01:00:12.150
She was a second-year resident.

01:00:13.818 --> 01:00:16.070
She couldn't sleep for days
after doing the test.

01:00:17.655 --> 01:00:18.865
She cried a lot.

01:00:20.241 --> 01:00:21.242
She sobbed and said

01:00:22.368 --> 01:00:23.953
she knew we couldn't save it.

01:00:24.954 --> 01:00:27.206
But she was hesitant to do it
to such a tiny body.

01:00:28.249 --> 01:00:29.792
She didn't want to cause any pain.

01:00:31.628 --> 01:00:32.629
After that incident,

01:00:34.005 --> 01:00:35.965
her heart would race
whenever she saw a baby.

01:00:36.466 --> 01:00:38.301
She couldn't even look at pregnant women.

01:00:40.970 --> 01:00:42.472
That's why I'm hesitant.

01:00:47.602 --> 01:00:49.437
It's not that I don't want to do it.

01:00:57.278 --> 01:00:58.321
I felt the same way.

01:01:01.074 --> 01:01:02.659
At 20 weeks…

01:01:05.495 --> 01:01:07.121
It really looked like a baby, you know?

01:01:09.499 --> 01:01:12.752
When it first came out,
it took a few last breaths.

01:01:14.337 --> 01:01:17.173
It even moved a bit
right there in my hands.

01:01:21.552 --> 01:01:23.221
It was truly terrifying.

01:01:27.016 --> 01:01:28.017
But what can we do?

01:01:29.394 --> 01:01:30.228
Still…

01:01:30.812 --> 01:01:31.813
We have to do it.

01:01:32.814 --> 01:01:34.232
That's why we're here.

01:01:40.780 --> 01:01:44.325
There is a cheat code I use
when I'm scared and terrified.

01:01:51.958 --> 01:01:53.793
I'm not sure if you have it though.

01:01:57.463 --> 01:02:01.134
DELIVERY ROOM 2

01:02:14.188 --> 01:02:15.857
DELIVERY ROOM 1

01:02:37.378 --> 01:02:39.964
The professor asked me
to relay the message again.

01:02:40.047 --> 01:02:42.717
She said you need to take
about 1 cm of the baby's skin tissue.

01:02:42.800 --> 01:02:45.470
If you put it in this container,
I'll submit it to DLM right away.

01:02:45.553 --> 01:02:46.929
DEPARTMENT OF LABORATORY MEDICINE

01:02:56.564 --> 01:02:57.482
Should we begin?

01:03:00.568 --> 01:03:01.402
Wait.

01:03:02.820 --> 01:03:05.698
It moved a bit back there.

01:03:05.782 --> 01:03:07.408
It even breathed slightly.

01:03:08.409 --> 01:03:09.327
That can happen.

01:03:10.787 --> 01:03:14.665
But a 20-week-old baby
can't be saved even with CPR.

01:03:14.749 --> 01:03:16.793
The organs aren't mature enough
to sustain life.

01:03:16.876 --> 01:03:18.336
Spontaneous breathing is impossible.

01:03:18.419 --> 01:03:19.253
But…

01:03:21.297 --> 01:03:24.509
What if I'm wrong and this is a mistake?

01:03:38.815 --> 01:03:40.858
This isn't from a textbook, but…

01:03:40.942 --> 01:03:44.237
I thought of something
since you said you were scared.

01:03:47.698 --> 01:03:50.326
CURRENT TIME

01:03:52.328 --> 01:03:56.207
May 17, 2023, 6:12 p.m.

01:03:56.290 --> 01:03:57.625
A beautiful baby

01:03:58.960 --> 01:04:00.962
went to a better place.

01:04:13.391 --> 01:04:14.392
Your mom said…

01:04:17.770 --> 01:04:19.021
she'd be waiting for you.

01:04:30.241 --> 01:04:31.492
Heal your wounds…

01:04:34.287 --> 01:04:35.621
in heaven.

01:04:37.999 --> 01:04:39.500
Then come back healthy again.

01:04:47.592 --> 01:04:48.426
I'm sorry.

01:05:23.461 --> 01:05:25.713
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

01:05:34.805 --> 01:05:36.933
HWANGBO
SUPERVISING PROFESSOR: SEO JUNG-MIN

01:05:39.769 --> 01:05:40.770
What are you doing here?

01:05:42.396 --> 01:05:44.148
You didn't have to come in person.

01:05:45.566 --> 01:05:46.776
This is the second time.

01:05:47.693 --> 01:05:49.111
For both her and you.

01:05:51.489 --> 01:05:53.741
It's always better to have company
when you're scared.

01:05:56.494 --> 01:05:57.328
You're right.

01:05:58.996 --> 01:05:59.830
But…

01:06:02.208 --> 01:06:04.543
she's all alone once again.

01:06:11.467 --> 01:06:13.636
That's why I told you to come to CS.

01:06:21.310 --> 01:06:22.311
Go in.

01:06:23.854 --> 01:06:24.814
I will.

01:06:25.856 --> 01:06:27.233
And lighten up.

01:06:35.616 --> 01:06:36.450
Don't leave.

01:06:52.383 --> 01:06:55.803
The test wasn't painful
for the baby, was it?

01:06:55.886 --> 01:06:56.721
No.

01:06:57.430 --> 01:07:01.308
The biopsy was successful,
and we sent it for genetic testing.

01:07:01.934 --> 01:07:05.855
It's a specialized test, so it'll take
about a month to get the results.

01:07:09.859 --> 01:07:12.153
I'm sorry it had to be this way again,

01:07:12.236 --> 01:07:14.780
but recurring abnormalities

01:07:14.864 --> 01:07:17.116
may have genetic factors.

01:07:17.199 --> 01:07:19.869
So we need to check
for the possibility of recurrence.

01:07:21.746 --> 01:07:23.247
This is still considered childbirth,

01:07:23.330 --> 01:07:26.459
so breast milk may be produced,
or you might have breast engorgement.

01:07:27.043 --> 01:07:30.629
And due to hormonal changes,
she may experience postpartum depression.

01:07:30.713 --> 01:07:32.631
Please pay close attention to her.

01:07:33.758 --> 01:07:34.592
Okay.

01:07:36.469 --> 01:07:38.846
And, ma'am…

01:07:49.315 --> 01:07:52.860
Cry as much as you want today.

01:07:54.779 --> 01:07:55.946
Next time,

01:07:56.572 --> 01:07:58.324
let's make sure

01:07:58.407 --> 01:08:01.494
we hear a healthy, strong baby cry.

01:08:32.691 --> 01:08:34.860
Gosh, I'm so popular.

01:08:34.944 --> 01:08:36.237
I was less popular as an idol.

01:08:36.320 --> 01:08:37.154
What's that?

01:08:37.238 --> 01:08:38.906
Don't people line up for those bagels?

01:08:39.532 --> 01:08:40.366
Exactly.

01:08:41.575 --> 01:08:43.744
This is practically a proposal, isn't it?

01:08:45.329 --> 01:08:47.873
Are you sure we can eat that?
They were given to you.

01:08:49.041 --> 01:08:50.334
They were given to us.

01:08:51.210 --> 01:08:53.629
Right. I should've brought
some coffee too.

01:08:58.592 --> 01:09:00.302
I got them on a late night discount.

01:09:00.928 --> 01:09:02.346
Hey, that's my favorite.

01:09:04.765 --> 01:09:06.851
I heard you had a sweet tooth.

01:09:09.270 --> 01:09:10.479
If you prefer something else--

01:09:10.563 --> 01:09:11.564
You're right.

01:09:12.565 --> 01:09:13.691
Thank you, Doctor.

01:09:14.316 --> 01:09:15.192
You're welcome.

01:09:16.485 --> 01:09:18.028
Good work today.

01:09:18.112 --> 01:09:19.738
Thank you. I'll enjoy it.

01:09:20.531 --> 01:09:21.532
Thank you.

01:09:31.709 --> 01:09:33.294
-Hey.
-Yes?

01:09:36.046 --> 01:09:37.047
What is it?

01:09:38.549 --> 01:09:42.178
Don't tell anyone about Nurse Ju-yeon.

01:09:43.262 --> 01:09:45.389
Don't tell what? Did something happen?

01:09:45.472 --> 01:09:47.766
What? No, nothing happened.

01:09:47.850 --> 01:09:49.852
They're dancing in perfect coordination.

01:09:51.103 --> 01:09:52.354
Hey, aren't you hungry?

01:09:52.438 --> 01:09:53.439
I am.

01:09:53.522 --> 01:09:54.440
Should we eat…

01:09:55.524 --> 01:09:56.525
Never mind.

01:09:56.609 --> 01:09:57.568
We can eat together.

01:09:58.611 --> 01:10:00.196
Really? Seriously?

01:10:00.279 --> 01:10:02.907
What should we get?
What do you like? I like everything.

01:10:02.990 --> 01:10:04.241
But I'm on call.

01:10:04.325 --> 01:10:05.951
Who cares? We can eat here.

01:10:06.869 --> 01:10:07.953
Why are you so excited?

01:10:08.037 --> 01:10:11.415
How could I not be? We're eating together.
Hey, let's ask the others too.

01:10:11.999 --> 01:10:13.500
Hurry up. We don't have much time.

01:10:34.730 --> 01:10:35.940
-Thanks--
-Sorry--

01:10:40.527 --> 01:10:42.154
Thanks for staying this late.

01:10:43.489 --> 01:10:45.324
I didn't do much, really.

01:10:50.829 --> 01:10:52.289
I'm sorry, but don't ask why.

01:10:55.626 --> 01:10:58.128
Okay. I'm not curious anyway.

01:11:03.092 --> 01:11:04.176
Yi-young.

01:11:06.428 --> 01:11:07.429
Aren't you hungry?

01:11:09.765 --> 01:11:10.683
Well…

01:11:14.478 --> 01:11:17.564
Guys! We're going to get food.
Come join us. Okay?

01:11:17.648 --> 01:11:18.732
Should we?

01:11:30.577 --> 01:11:31.412
Let's go.

01:11:32.204 --> 01:11:33.122
Awesome!

01:11:35.749 --> 01:11:37.126
Are you really that happy?

01:11:37.209 --> 01:11:39.628
Yes! I always ate alone after work.

01:11:39.712 --> 01:11:43.257
Guys, let's get the most delicious dish
in the cafeteria.

01:11:43.340 --> 01:11:44.550
And what's that?

01:11:44.633 --> 01:11:46.260
-Bulgogi beef set!
-Bulgogi beef set!

01:11:46.343 --> 01:11:48.762
Nice! Let's go have some!

01:11:48.846 --> 01:11:50.014
-All right.
-Hurry up!

01:11:56.228 --> 01:11:57.062
My phone.

01:12:14.830 --> 01:12:16.290
Who's on duty today?

01:12:16.373 --> 01:12:18.167
-Dr. Pyo Nam-kyung.
-I see.

01:12:18.250 --> 01:12:19.752
We had four GYN patients at the ER,

01:12:19.835 --> 01:12:22.338
so she had a really tough time
making urgent calls.

01:12:22.421 --> 01:12:23.922
I told her to get some rest.

01:12:24.006 --> 01:12:24.923
Okay.

01:12:25.883 --> 01:12:27.509
Right, the professor said

01:12:27.593 --> 01:12:29.553
Ms. Cho Min-ae
could have small sips of water,

01:12:29.636 --> 01:12:31.055
but the order hasn't been entered.

01:12:31.138 --> 01:12:32.139
I see.

01:12:32.723 --> 01:12:36.185
She's sleeping anyway, so could you
please check on it before morning?

01:12:37.019 --> 01:12:40.356
Okay. I'll notify Dr. Pyo
about everything at once in the morning.

01:12:40.939 --> 01:12:43.025
-Let me check on Ms. Lee Hyo-sun.
-Sure.

01:12:49.948 --> 01:12:51.575
Pyo Nam-kyung speaking.

01:12:51.658 --> 01:12:54.370
Doctor, were you sleeping?

01:12:55.954 --> 01:12:57.664
Oh, I didn't know.

01:12:57.748 --> 01:13:00.626
It's about Ms. Cho Min-ae.

01:13:00.709 --> 01:13:02.920
The professor said
she could have water during rounds.

01:13:03.003 --> 01:13:04.546
Can she have some now?

01:13:05.381 --> 01:13:06.632
Yes, water.

01:13:08.759 --> 01:13:11.303
Okay. Please put in the order right away.

01:13:12.596 --> 01:13:13.639
Goodbye.

01:14:06.525 --> 01:14:10.737
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUEST,
JUNG KYUNG-HO, OUR ETERNAL KIM JUN-WAN

01:14:10.821 --> 01:14:14.199
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:14:14.283 --> 01:14:15.492
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

01:14:15.576 --> 01:14:17.494
Weren't you
in the Yulje OB-GYN get-together?

01:14:17.578 --> 01:14:19.621
Did you make any mistakes while drinking?

01:14:19.705 --> 01:14:22.040
Of course not. How old do you think I am?

01:14:22.124 --> 01:14:23.542
Don't, don't, don't.

01:14:23.625 --> 01:14:25.294
What?

01:14:25.377 --> 01:14:27.379
It's okay. I'm just really curious.

01:14:27.463 --> 01:14:28.422
That's interesting.

01:14:28.505 --> 01:14:29.840
What did I say about drinking?

01:14:29.923 --> 01:14:31.508
Did you watch your mouth or not?

01:14:32.509 --> 01:14:33.594
Did you get home safe?

01:14:37.389 --> 01:14:39.057
He failed today too.

01:14:39.141 --> 01:14:40.017
I'm sorry.

01:14:41.101 --> 01:14:42.978
The patients are upset.

01:14:43.061 --> 01:14:45.564
Professor Seo's patients
are taken care of. Why are mine not?

01:14:45.647 --> 01:14:47.483
What's wrong with you all?

01:14:47.566 --> 01:14:49.401
I'll check on it. I'm sorry.

01:14:49.485 --> 01:14:52.738
It's unlike them to miss things.
I'll scold them properly today.

01:14:52.821 --> 01:14:54.740
Does she think
you have nothing better to do?

01:14:54.823 --> 01:14:56.575
Aren't you here to ask me for a favor too?

01:14:56.658 --> 01:14:58.202
Would the workload be too much then?

01:14:59.661 --> 01:15:02.122
I did make a mistake,
but he said he couldn't do it.

01:15:02.206 --> 01:15:04.082
The least he could've done was keep quiet.

01:15:04.166 --> 01:15:05.334
Can't you control your anger?

01:15:05.417 --> 01:15:07.544
-Do you have to lash out to feel better?
-Yes.

01:15:07.628 --> 01:15:08.462
Hey!

01:15:10.047 --> 01:15:12.549
Wasting others' time
because you won't take responsibility…

01:15:13.550 --> 01:15:14.426
That's incompetence.

01:15:24.061 --> 01:15:26.063
Subtitle translation by: Sooji Kim
